Callgrind
---------
Source: https://web.stanford.edu/class/archive/cs/cs107/cs107.1222/lab7/

`objdump -d ./trials` prints the disassembly to stdout.

Running

`valgrind --tool=callgrind ./trials`

creates a `callgrind.out.<pid>` file that you can run the following command on:

`valgrind-annotate --auto=yes callgrind.out.<pid>` 

This shows instruction counts of the different implementations for powers of 2. The greater the instruction count, the more time it's assumed to take. 
